# Baseline table specification — candidate for human review

Status: proposed output specification; no confirmed formal version. This retains the already confirmed analysis population of all eligible adults.

The table has exactly two treatment columns, Treatment A followed by Treatment B. Each heading includes its own total group N. Rows appear in this order: Age (years), Female sex, BMI (kg/m²). Continuous values use mean (SD), each to one decimal place. Female sex uses n (%) with the count as an integer and percentage to one decimal place. Use a compact table without significance tests or p-value columns.

For each variable, exclude only that variable's missing values from its summary and denominator. The group heading N remains the full group size. Report missing counts separately by variable and treatment group in a table-wide footnote. In the simulated example, Female sex is 3/5=60.0% in A and 2/4=50.0% in B; the heading Ns remain 6 and 5.

Recommended implementation convention for review: calculate sample SD using n−1. This detail is proposed here; it is not a separately confirmed project decision. No real data or variable dictionary were supplied, so source-variable mappings, actual group sizes and actual missingness cannot yet be verified. No empirical values are claimed by this candidate.

## Simulated review example

All displayed values below are invented for presentation review. Confirming the format does not confirm these numbers as results. The formal table will use observed study values after the specification is confirmed and data mappings are verified.

```table
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "baseline-table-simulated-preview",
  "title": "Table 1. Baseline characteristics — SIMULATED EXAMPLE ONLY",
  "simulated": true,
  "columns": [
    {
      "id": "a",
      "label": "Treatment A (N=6)",
      "align": "right"
    },
    {
      "id": "b",
      "label": "Treatment B (N=5)",
      "align": "right"
    }
  ],
  "headers": [
    {
      "id": "header-a",
      "label": "Treatment A (N=6)",
      "column_id": "a"
    },
    {
      "id": "header-b",
      "label": "Treatment B (N=5)",
      "column_id": "b"
    }
  ],
  "rows": [
    {
      "id": "age",
      "label": "Age (years)",
      "cells": {
        "a": "60.0 (15.8)",
        "b": "60.0 (12.9)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "female",
      "label": "Female sex",
      "cells": {
        "a": "3 (60.0%)",
        "b": "2 (50.0%)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bmi",
      "label": "BMI (kg/m²)",
      "cells": {
        "a": "24.0 (3.2)",
        "b": "25.0 (3.7)"
      }
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [
    {
      "id": "simulated",
      "text": "SIMULATED VALUES: invented solely to review the layout; these are not study results."
    },
    {
      "id": "summary",
      "text": "Continuous variables: mean (SD), one decimal; Female sex: n (%) with one decimal for percentage. SD in this preview is sample SD (n−1)."
    },
    {
      "id": "denominator",
      "text": "Each heading N is the full number in that treatment group. Missing values are excluded separately for each variable from its summary and denominator; there is no complete-case exclusion across variables."
    },
    {
      "id": "missing",
      "text": "Missing counts (Treatment A / Treatment B): Age 1 / 1; Female sex 1 / 1; BMI 1 / 1."
    }
  ]
}
```

